<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96767" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στῐβᾰρ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>strong, stout, sturdy</i>, freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
			</span></i>, of men's limbs, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦμος, αὐχήν,
				βραχίονες</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.400
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.415
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χείρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					8.189
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					76
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλευραί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					111
				</span></i>
			; of weapons, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγχος, σάκος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.746
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.335
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίσκος -ώτερος</span>
			<i>more massy</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.187
			</span></i>; later, of persons, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τις καὶ καρτερά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					639
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τὸ σῶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					6.2.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῇ γλώσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ez.</u>
					3.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοῖρα ς</span>. Epigr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				10.12.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπίη</span> (of Aeschylus) <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.39
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antip.Thess.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπειλά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hymm.Is.</u>
					170
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Th.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Comp.</u>
				22
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος λόγος</span> a
				<i>bulkier</i> book, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυμνάσια -ώτερα, -ώτατα</span>,
				<i>more</i> (<i>most</i>) <i>violent</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.21.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.35.2
			</span></i>. Adv., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύλαι . . πύκα
				-ρῶς ἀραρυῖαι</span> gates <i>close</i> shut, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.454
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρύνων τὸν κλοιὸν ς</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Hb.</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρόντιζε ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				2.5
			</span></i>. (Prob. cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στείβω</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
